# ============================================================================
#  What is deliberately NOT committed, and why.
#
#  The rule this repo follows: commit the GENERATOR, never its output, and
#  never anything a documented command reproduces. Everything ignored below is
#  either rebuilt by a script in docker/ or scripts/, or is an editor artefact.
# ============================================================================

# ---- Chrono SDK: 1.2 GB, exported from the container -----------------------
# Produced by `bash docker/03-export-sdk.sh` and `bash docker/04-build-shim.sh`
# from the chrono:10.0.0 image. Binary, huge, and machine-specific: it is built
# -march=skylake, so a copy from another host would be wrong as well as large.
/chrono-sdk/

# ---- Unreal build artefacts ------------------------------------------------
# Regenerated by Build.sh. Intermediate alone is ~150 MB.
SimA/Intermediate/
SimA/Binaries/
SimA/Saved/
SimA/DerivedDataCache/
SimA/Build/
SimA/.vscode/
SimA/Plugins/*/Intermediate/
SimA/Plugins/*/Binaries/
# Generated by UnrealBuildTool with ABSOLUTE paths to this machine's engine
# install, so it is actively wrong on any other host.
SimA/Makefile
SimA/*.code-workspace
SimA/*.uproject.user

*.VC.db
*.opensdf
*.sdf
*.suo

# ---- Host test harness build directories -----------------------------------
# Each of these is `bash <dir>/run.sh build` away.
driver/build/
referee/build/
mirror/build/
ring/build/
cockpit/build/
wheel/build/
vehicle/build/
shim/build/

# ---- Generated data that a generator owns ----------------------------------
# EXCEPTION worth stating: vehicle/innova/*.json, course/simA_course.json,
# course/simA_terrain.txt and course/simA_referee.txt ARE committed, even
# though gen_innova.py and gen_course.py produce them. They are small, they are
# read by three different consumers (physics, referee, renderer), and having
# them in the tree means a fresh clone can run the host test suite without a
# container. `bash course/run.sh check` fails if they drift from the generator.

# ---- Editor / OS noise -----------------------------------------------------
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# ---- Local logs and scratch ------------------------------------------------
*.log
/tmp/
